8</doc-number> <kind>A</kind> </document-id> <sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9057782-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9057782</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1151840A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUJII ATSUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IDEMITSU PETROCHEMICAL CO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UCHIYAMA KATSUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJII, ATSUSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IDEMITSU PETROCHEMICAL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UCHIYAMA, KATSUMI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUJII ATSUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UCHIYAMA KATSUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJII, ATSUSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UCHIYAMA, KATSUMI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A polyolefine foam sheet production method using a device having first and second heating rolls (62, 63) and provided with an endless belt (65) passed around the rolls and rotated, wherein a foaming base sheet (69) is brought into contact with the first roll (62) via the belt (65) and heated at temperatures not lower than a temperature to permit thermocompression-bonding to the belt (65) and lower than a foaming initiation temperature to thermocompression-bond the sheet (69) to the belt (65); then the sheet (69) is brought into contact with the second roll (63) via the belt (65) and heated for foaming at temperatures not lower than a foaming initiation temperature to form a foam sheet (61), whereby stretching/shrinking and wrinkling of the foam sheet at heating/foaming can be prevented.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé de production d'une feuille de mousse polyoléfinique, consistant à utiliser un dispositif qui comporte un premier et un second rouleau de chauffage (62, 63) et est pourvu d'une bande sans fin (65) passant autour des rouleaux et mise en rotation, à mettre en contact une feuille de base de moussage (69) avec le premier rouleau (62), au moyen de la bande (65), et à chauffer cette feuille à des températures non inférieures à une température permettant une liaison par thermocompression avec la bande (65), et inférieures à une température de démarrage de moussage permettant la liaison par thermocompression de la feuille (69) avec la bande (65), puis à mettre la feuille (69) en contact avec le second rouleau (63), au moyen de la bande (65), et à chauffer cette feuille aux fins de moussage, à des températures non inférieures à une température de démarrage du moussage, afin de former une feuille en mousse (61), de sorte que l'on empêche ainsi l'étirage/rétrécissement et le plissement de la feuille en mousse lors du chauffage/moussage.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>